  "does_not_prove": [
    "that jcc_core is restarted after a reboot. No component in this repository restarts the service if it dies: scripts/service-watchdog.ps1 monitors the release state and the port, and the operator starts the service. Recorded in artifacts/acceptance/REBOOT_RECOVERY.json and in artifacts/release/PROJECT_RUN_READINESS.md, not papered over here.",
    "that F-03's regeneration requirement is checked by the gate. The gate accepts this manifest on presence alone and says so in its own detail string; the regeneration check is `--verify` in this script, and its result is recorded under `regeneration_check` below.",
    "that this tool verified the scheduled task JEV-JCC-Continuation-Watchdog through the scheduler API. The task IS registered on this host and fires every 2 minutes -- its own on-disk definition is Enabled=true with a PT2M repetition under principal S-1-5-18, and the watchdog's tick log gains exactly one line every 120 s -- but the agent sandbox cannot enumerate Task Scheduler through CIM (Get-ScheduledTask fails there), so registration rests on the task's own definition plus its tick interval, not on a live query from here. This entry previously claimed the task was NOT registered, which repeated the sandbox's silence as a fact about the host."
  ],
